{title: More Love to Thee}
{artist: Elizabeth Prentiss & William Doane}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 72}

Verse 1
[Eb]More love to [Bb]thee, O [Eb]Christ, more [Ab]love to [Bb]thee!
[Eb]Hear thou the [Bb]prayer I [Cm]make on [Ab]bended [Bb]knee;
[Eb]this is my [Bb]earnest [Eb]plea: more [Ab]love, O [Eb]Christ, to [Bb]thee —
[Eb]more love to [Ab]thee, [Eb]more [Bb]love to [Eb]thee!

Verse 2
[Eb]Once earthly joy [Bb]I craved, [Eb]Sought peace [Ab]and rest; [Bb]Now
[Eb]thee alone I [Bb]seek, Give [Cm]what is [Ab]best; [Bb]This
[Eb]all my pray'r [Bb]shall [Eb]be, More [Ab]love, [Eb]O Christ, [Bb]to Thee,
[Eb]More love to [Ab]Thee; [Eb]More [Bb]love to [Eb]Thee.

Verse 3
[Eb]Then shall my [Bb]latest [Eb]breath, Whisper [Ab]Thy praise, [Bb]This
[Eb]be the parting [Bb]cry My [Cm]heart shall [Ab]raise; [Bb]This
[Eb]still its pray'r [Bb]shall [Eb]be, More [Ab]love, [Eb]O Christ, [Bb]to Thee,
[Eb]More love to [Ab]Thee; [Eb]More [Bb]love to [Eb]Thee.
